1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,184
PACT.

2
00:00:01,184 --> 00:00:04,483
Partition-Aware Coordination for Transport.

3
00:00:04,483 --> 00:00:09,624
A drone delivery fleet that keeps working when the brain goes dark.

4
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:17,864
Today's delivery fleets depend on one central controller and an unbroken radio link.

5
00:00:17,864 --> 00:00:20,763
Lose the hub, and every drone stops.

6
00:00:20,763 --> 00:00:26,239
Split the radio, and two groups of drones can claim the same parcel.

7
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,563
In PACT, there is no central controller.

8
00:00:31,563 --> 00:00:38,171
Every drone runs the same logic, and talks only to the drones within radio range.

9
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:43,311
Drones bid for jobs on priority, distance, deadline and energy.

10
00:00:43,311 --> 00:00:49,755
Each one keeps its own copy of the order board, and the copies merge by gossip.

11
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:58,114
Here is the same city, the same seed and the same orders, twice.

12
00:00:58,114 --> 00:01:01,779
On the left, a central hub assigns every job.

13
00:01:01,779 --> 00:01:04,549
At three minutes, we kill the hub.

14
00:01:04,549 --> 00:01:07,808
The central fleet stops taking new work.

15
00:01:07,808 --> 00:01:12,451
PACT has nothing central to lose, so it keeps delivering:

16
00:01:12,451 --> 00:01:17,420
eighty-six percent on time, the same as with no fault at all.

17
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:26,528
Now the radio splits the fleet in two for five minutes.

18
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:33,716
Each side keeps working under a partition policy, and every claim carries an epoch and a lease.

19
00:01:33,716 --> 00:01:37,347
A depot hands a parcel only to the newest owner.

20
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:43,854
Across two hundred and forty runs with radio splits, PACT made zero double deliveries.

21
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:47,258
A plain auction made nearly eighteen per run.

22
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:57,288
When a drone fails in the middle of a delivery, it simply goes silent.

23
00:01:57,288 --> 00:02:07,692
The drones that expected to hear it report the silence, its depot declares it failed, and exactly one replacement job is auctioned to another drone.

24
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:18,587
The same protocol also runs as real robotics software:

25
00:02:18,587 --> 00:02:31,798
ROS 2 lifecycle components, one container per drone, quadrotor physics in Gazebo, and PX4 autopilots in the loop, over an authenticated mesh radio.

26
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,548
Every run is deterministic.

27
00:02:41,548 --> 00:02:48,959
The same seed gives the same event log, and the replay viewer verifies it event by event.

28
00:02:48,959 --> 00:02:58,201
Nearly a thousand automated tests pass across both simulators, with a public benchmark against three baselines.

29
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:06,147
PACT is a simulation prototype today, and real hardware is the next step.

30
00:03:06,147 --> 00:03:06,746
No hub.

31
00:03:06,746 --> 00:03:08,371
No double delivery.

32
00:03:08,371 --> 00:03:09,142
No stall.

